Explaining to another Junior developer:
                                      Imagine you're managing a todo list and need to know which task to work on next. Instead of just looking at priority,
                                      this algorithm scores each task by combining multiple factors like how urgent the deadline is, whether it's already done,
                                      and if it has a "blocker" tag. Think of it like a weighted voting system where different factors contribute different amounts
                                      to a final score. The code multiplies priority by 10 to give it weight, adds bonuses for tasks due soon or recently updated, 
                                      and subtracts points for completed work so you don't waste time re-prioritizing done tasks. Then it sorts everything by that 
                                      final score, highest first.
